  "worked_solution": "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sec}^{2}\u2061(x)+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}\u2061(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(x)+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(x)){|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061\\frac{\\pi }{3})-(\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061\\frac{\\pi /3}{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
